    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract base for the <ref refid="class_s_l_p" kindref="compound">SLP</ref> evaluator hierarchy. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holds an <computeroutput>SLProgram*</computeroutput> plus iterators into its gate arrays and declares the pure-virtual interface (<computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_l_evaluator_a1ba1b2c62ac765657c09e9bab3cc38c2_1a1ba1b2c62ac765657c09e9bab3cc38c2" kindref="member">evaluate</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_l_evaluator_a4841809208f36e3a4c50bb09b869e6a7_1a4841809208f36e3a4c50bb09b869e6a7" kindref="member">specialize</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_l_evaluator_a0dff6157c449c84f695e269341997d60_1a0dff6157c449c84f695e269341997d60" kindref="member">createHomotopy</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_l_evaluator_aaa10a6eb4df0c5cbaec90f50aa30396e_1aaa10a6eb4df0c5cbaec90f50aa30396e" kindref="member">text_out</ref></computeroutput>) used by interpreter callers. Concrete arithmetic happens in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_l_evaluator_concrete" kindref="compound">SLEvaluatorConcrete</ref>&lt;RT&gt;</computeroutput>, which carries the <computeroutput>std::vector&lt;RT::ElementType&gt;</computeroutput> of node values and (optionally) a compiled function pointer. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
